    "id": "01a1d168-39c1-7698-a7f6-baa8465a06de",
    "name": "Coaching & Mentorship",
    "description": "Ann Arbor SPARK is committed to assisting startups as they navigate the challenges of entrepreneurship. One of our core values is to educate entrepreneurs and provide tools to propel early-stage businesses in driving industries such as tech, life sciences, and mobility. Clients who have benefited from our free services have experienced accelerated growth and greater success. Whether your company is in its infancy or your team is seeking mentorship to take your new business to the next level, we offer a range of supportive services and resources.\n\nInterested in becoming a SPARK client? Complete our intake form and a SPARK team member will follow up with you. We are eager to connect and engage. \n\nAs founders bring their ideas to life, there is a wealth of ways to formulate your business. It’s important that startups have the relevant information needed to make their business a reality. Similarly, connecting with others in the community — from first-time entrepreneurs to those with decades of experience — can grow your network. Fortunately, SPARK offers a host of educational resources and networking events to boost your skillset and broaden your contacts.\n\nStrategic marketing support is one of the most requested services by SPARK clients. Our in-house expert consults with startups on effectively reaching their targeted audience through intentional, tactical actions. \n\nEvery startup journey is unique and specific challenges require targeted solutions. Ann Arbor SPARK advisors can confidentially coach you through pain points and connect you to client resources, including:       \n\nEven after a company has established itself, maintaining consistent growth and achieving development milestones are important for maturing a business. These services are targeted toward moving your company forward and giving your business the edge it needs to remain competitive.\n\nWith funds earmarked by the Michigan Economic Development Corporation and budget oversight provided by the Ann Arbor/Ypsilanti SmartZone Local Development Finance Authority (LDFA), Ann Arbor SPARK’s entrepreneurial programs, services, tools, and resources support the growth of a vibrant startup ecosystem.",
