  {
    "id": "01a1d168-333c-7011-ab96-542b8ea74d37",
    "name": "Progress Over Perfection: Knowing When It’s Good Enough to Launch, a 20Fathoms Breakfast Lab",
    "description": "This week at Breakfast Lab:\n\nHow do you decide when something is ready to put in front of customers? Jack Rutkowski, inventor of Flabocce, will use the original assembly and materials of Flabocce’s tiebreaker tool, plus the packaging he still uses today, to walk through how he thought about launching with room to improve. You’ll hear why some of his early choices still hold up, what’s motivating the next change, and how to decide what needs your attention now.\n\nWe’ll Cover:\n\nDefining a workable first version: what the original tiebreaker tool needed to accomplish, and the compromises built into its assembly and materials\n\nDeciding what earns an upgrade: why Jack still uses the original packaging, and what’s motivating the next change\n\nApplying the lesson: identify something you’re holding back, define an acceptable first version, and decide what would justify improving it\n\nAbout the Presenter\n\nJack Rutkowski invented Flabocce and is a product and content developer based in Traverse City. His background spans media production and wellness: he partnered with P90X creative director Ned Farr to produce fitness content and testimonials for brands like Beachbody and Gaiam, and spent years as a voice-over artist for ads on Pandora Internet Radio.\n\nWhat is Breakfast Lab?\n\nBreakfast Lab is a weekly event at 20Fathoms where you’ll get expert guidance to help meet your most pressing startup needs, providing access to the right tools and the right people at the right time.\n\nThese events are held in person and will be offered virtually. There is no cost to attend. Coffee and a light breakfast are provided. Walk-ins are welcome.\n\nAnd if you’d like to stay and keep working, coworking at 20Fathoms is free on Thursdays for Breakfast Lab attendees.\n\nLearn more about Breakfast Lab.\n\nAbout 20Fathoms:\n\n20Fathoms is the home of entrepreneurship and innovation in Northwest Michigan. Based in Traverse City and serving all of Northwest Lower Michigan, 20Fathoms is a nonprofit startup incubator and resource center for entrepreneurs and growing businesses. The organization works with entrepreneurs of all stages and industries, and specializes in working with technology-focused companies. Programs include startup education, business coaching, connections, funding, and general support.",
    "url": "https://20fathoms.org/event/progress-over-perfection-knowing-when-its-good-enough-to-launch-a-20fathoms-breakfast-lab/",
    "startsAt": "2026-11-19T14:00:00.000Z",
    "endsAt": "2026-11-19T15:30:00.000Z",
